    <article class="notice-content">
        <h2>About this study</h2>
        <p>E-Waste Connect is a university study of e-waste coordination in Nairobi County. It is not an official county or regulator service. Use synthetic data for evaluation.</p>
        <h2>Information used for account access</h2>
        <p>We store your email, optional display name, a password hash, account status, role and the version and date of your notice acknowledgment. Account information supports sign-in, access control and password recovery. Session cookies maintain your sign-in; recovery links expire after 60 minutes.</p>
        <h2>Device and collection requests</h2>
        <p>Owned device identities and self-reports support tracking. Collection requests retain selected item identities, estimated mass, preferred dates and request history. Private contact/address draft fields are encrypted in the server session; submitted contact/address and change reasons are encrypted at rest. Precise pickup coordinates are restricted to your owned request. Requests remain awaiting review; this acknowledgment does not authorize a physical handover or guarantee service.</p>
        <p>Other consumers, collectors and processors cannot access your private requests in this increment. Future assignment-scoped access needs its own authorized workflow. Synthetic study points and geometry do not confirm real collection acceptance. No external request notification is sent.</p>
        <h2>Optional pickup maps and browser location</h2>
        <p>Loading the pickup map contacts the configured external tile provider (OpenStreetMap by default). Tile requests reveal your IP address, browser information, this site's origin and the approximate area you view. They do not include your name, contact details, address text, request reference or literal pickup coordinates. The tile provider may infer an approximate location from the tiles viewed. OpenStreetMap service use is covered by the <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenStreetMap Foundation privacy policy</a>.</p>
        <p>Use my location requests browser location only when you press it. Your browser controls permission and may use its own location services. Reported accuracy is approximate; verify the meeting point and confirm it. No background tracking is used. You can use Advanced location entry without loading external tiles or granting location permission. Precise selections stay in the encrypted server draft and your restricted request details; they are not saved to browser persistent storage.</p>
        <h2>Access and security</h2>
        <p>Passwords are hashed. Recovery tokens are stored as hashes. Authorized project administrators control staff provisioning. Security records use account identifiers without password or recovery-token contents. Local evaluation recovery messages remain private to the project operator.</p>
        <h2>Evaluation and retention</h2>
        <p>Synthetic data is the default. Any evaluator personal data must be collected with informed permission and removed within 90 days after assessment, following the study retention policy. Account information is used for this study and is not sold.</p>
        <h2>Questions and account information</h2>
        <p>Contact the researcher through the study contact provided with your evaluation invitation about access, correction or deletion. Self-service privacy requests are not yet available. Acknowledging this notice records that you have read it; it does not authorize new uses of your information.</p>
        <p class="hint">Notice version {{ $noticeVersion }} is retained with each Consumer registration.</p>
    </article>
